# O10-HYGIENE acceptance (Familiarity, criterion 2): the state after the change. Every check must pass; none is a known failure.
F0 the Familiarity row offers Familiar, A mix and Discover (the labels are unchanged)
F1 an unset Familiarity shows "A mix", not "Familiar"
F1b the other unset moods still show their neutral choice (Energy Any, Voices Any, Range Any)
F1c the precondition holds: the fixture station really has no Familiarity stored
F2 merely showing an unset station writes nothing
F3 the unset Familiarity stays "A mix" across poll re-renders
F4 choosing Familiar on an unset station stores Familiar
F4b ... and the row then shows Familiar
F4c choosing Discover stores New and shows Discover
F4d choosing A mix shows A mix again
F5 a stored Familiarity of 'Familiar' shows 'Familiar'
F5 a stored Familiarity of 'Any' shows 'A mix'
F5 a stored Familiarity of 'New' shows 'Discover'
F6 a station with only Energy set shows Calm and an unset Familiarity of "A mix"
